00:09:02.183 --> 00:09:06.216
<v Host>Time for a short quiz. Listen and try to answer.

00:09:06.816 --> 00:09:13.344
<v Slow>エンジンの燃焼試験は、どこで行われましたか。

00:09:14.144 --> 00:09:18.440
<v Host>At the Tanegashima Space Center in Kagoshima Prefecture.

00:09:19.039 --> 00:09:25.087
<v Slow>エンジンは、何秒間、燃え続けましたか。

00:09:25.888 --> 00:09:29.751
<v Host>About one hundred thirty seconds, just as planned.

00:09:30.351 --> 00:09:37.696
<v Slow>JAXAは、いつまでに1号機の打ち上げを目指していますか。

00:09:38.495 --> 00:09:43.344
<v Host>Within fiscal twenty twenty-six — by the end of March twenty twenty-seven.

00:09:43.943 --> 00:10:08.495
<v Host>That's all for today. On July twenty-third, Japan's space agency successfully completed the last major ground test of the Epsilon S rocket's second-stage engine at Tanegashima, after explosions in twenty twenty-three and twenty twenty-four had delayed the project. The first launch is now planned within this fiscal year. Thanks for listening, and see you tomorrow.

00:10:09.096 --> 00:10:11.495
<v News>また明日。
